   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Intransitivity and the impersonal passive with dative",
     "texto": [
      "In German only accusative complements have the syntactic capacity to be promoted to the nominative subject in the passive. Verbs that select exclusively a dative complement (**helfen, danken, widersprechen**) cannot generate a passive with a personal subject: forms such as *Ich wurde geholfen* are incorrect; one must say **Mir wurde geholfen** or **Ihm wurde widersprochen**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Bitransitive verbs (Dative + Accusative)",
     "texto": [
      "When the verb simultaneously admits an accusative of thing and a dative of person (**geben, überreichen, mitteilen**), the accusative object is transformed into the nominative subject of the passive, while the dative of person remains unchanged in its original dative case: **Der Bescheid wurde dem Antragsteller zugestellt** (the notice was delivered to the applicant)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Original case",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Reaction in the passive voice",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Canonical example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "Dative only (helfen)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Invariable dative without nominative subject",
